    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$ at $\\left(2,\\dfrac14\\right)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x+4y-3=0$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=x^{-2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-2x^{-3}=-\\frac{2}{x^3}\\\\m&=-\\frac{2}{2^3}=-\\frac14\\end{aligned}$$\nUsing $y-y_1=m(x-x_1)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac14&=-\\frac14(x-2)\\\\4y-1&=-x+2\\\\x+4y-3&=0\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
